+## TD-9001: A team whose only live sessions are its seats offers Start, and the Start leaves each live seat running
+
+**Priority:** Medium
+**Type:** debt
+**Added:** 2026-11-14
+**Owner:** grinder
+**Kind:** build
+**Status:** Open
+**Blocked by:** decision (paul)
+**Part of:** TD-1569
+**Location:** design §4.9a A Start beside a busy seat, §4.5a team card: Start / Wind down / Stop now; src/sessionorc/work.py (finished); src/shiftlead/teamrun.py (rows, start, standing_seats, keep_mail_for); src/sessionorc/agent_tick.py (_mark_team_start); src/shiftlead/ui/repo.py, src/shiftlead/ui/templates/group_head.html (the team card), src/shiftlead/ui/app.py (the start press's toast), src/shiftlead/ui/static/app.js (the Start anyway dialog), src/shiftlead/ui/org.py (the rollup's acts), src/shiftlead/ui/help.py; src/shiftlead/cli.py (ao team list)
+
+**Why:** TD-1569's first half: a team whose members are down while a seat of it is still at work (ao-grind, 2026-11-10: the techlead idle with a background merge running, the grinders and designer down with work in their lanes) has no Start on its card, and `ao team start` refuses on the seat's name.
+
+**Ask:** Go on this build as written, now that TD-1569's four review rounds have ended at the cap (One more round recommended: F91's fix, the suspended verdict never rebuilt, is read by no review)?
+
+**Fix:** Build design §4.9a *A Start beside a busy seat*, §4.9 *Starting and stopping* and *Start reads the same pairing*, §4.5a's rows *team card: Start / Wind down / Stop now*, *team groups* and *rollup: press and menus*, §4.7 *Teams*:
+- `work.finished` returns **`clauses: {<name>: <clause without the name>}`** beside `why`, the same text keyed by the record's name (or id), for every session it gives a clause; `why` is unchanged, so the tick and the page read as before.
+- **`teamrun.standing_seats(team, mine)`**, a new function read by `members_down` and the start's set-aside alone (`seat_names` and `_seat_of` unchanged): a live crew record under the name the definition gives it now — the techlead, a seat with a trigger, the manager on call in the definition now and carrying its `seat` mark — or an extra of one of those seats (`scale` and a `seat` mark both, `scale.line` the techlead's or a trigger seat's name in the definition now). A worker line's extra (`scale`, no `seat` mark), a seat the definition renamed or dropped, one under a stale tmux suffix, and the Settings sweeper are not standing seats.
+- `teamrun.rows` carries **`members_down`**: None, or `{seats: [{name, id, why}]}` with one entry per live seat when the team has a live unattended session, every such session is a standing seat, none suspended, and `concluded` is None — `why` from `clauses`, else the record's state; None wherever `concluded` holds (concluded wins). `ao team list --json` carries it, and its text prints *members down: <seat> (<why>)*, seats joined by `, `, where it prints *concluded*.
+- `teamrun.start`, in this order: the name checks for every launch; the `list` read every Start makes for the pairing; where a verdict is `live` or `suspended` or the pairing found a rename or a removal (as today's `_close_concluded` is reached), the team's reading with `waiting_of_home(call, strict=True)` — the existing reads restructured so the left seats are decided before `keep_mail_for`; on a concluded team `_close_concluded` as today (its idle seats closed); otherwise each `live` verdict whose holder is a live standing seat is set aside as left — its create skipped, the holder not closed, typed at or superseded, and left out of `keep_mail_for`'s verdicts — a `live` verdict whose holder the read finds dead (any holder, on this path; a `suspended` verdict is never rebuilt and refuses) is rebuilt from the read as the dead record's verdict (`supersede` with its `holder_state`, no second name check), given to `keep_mail_for` as the dead holder it now is (its mail kept where any dead holder's is: closed, or exited with `stop_held`), and goes to its create (superseded as §4.1 does), and any other `live` or `suspended` holder raises `NamesHeld` (TD-9002's words), naming those holders and not the seats. `_pairing` and `_start_moves` are unchanged (Apply and the card's rename lines read them): a running orphan (a renamed, dropped or stale-suffixed live seat) refuses as today; a live Settings sweeper holds its name as any non-standing live session does. A failed strict `waiting` read refuses as today. A session's start (`caller` set) that would leave a seat is refused, only where nothing else refused, in its own words: *team <t> was not started — <seat> is running: a Start that leaves a seat running is a person's (design §4.9a A Start beside a busy seat)*. Where the left seat is the manager on call, its id is `lead_id`: the techlead's, each seat's and each member's `controllers`, `write_extras`' controllers, `out_of_reach` and the result's `manager` read it. The result gains `left: [{name, id, why}]`, the seats whose launch was skipped.
+- `agent_tick._mark_team_start` passes over a live seat (a record carrying `seat`) when it asks whether an unattended record of the team runs, so a members-down Start writes the usage mark as a start from nothing live does. It holds for every start: a Start from nothing live writes the mark at every create until a member is live, and rule 8's replay of one member beside a live seat writes it too.
+- The Sessions page (`src/shiftlead/ui/repo.py`'s team rows, `src/shiftlead/ui/templates/group_head.html`) draws a third header state for a team whose row has `members_down` — its words *members down · <seat> <why>*, seats joined by ` · `, Start, Wind down and Stop now in that order, the team's work note as on a stopped card, the *i* panel's *not concluded* line still drawn (why the team is not concluded), `stopped` staying `not live or concluded` — with the live team's existing *definition changed* / *flow changed* Apply mark where the records differ; `members_down` is held to the records as `concluded` is (its seats' names the live names), neither drawn where they disagree; the one-line confirm names every live seat from `members_down.seats` (*Start ao-grind? techlead-ao-1 (idle, shell live) and review-ao-1 (working) are left running*), the rename lines first, and the empty-lanes Start anyway dialog carries the seats as its second line, as a concluded team's carries its closes. The rollup row's ⋯ (`src/shiftlead/ui/org.py`, its `acts`) holds Start after Wind down and Stop now on such a team.
+- Two help paragraphs, each in §4.5a's list and `src/shiftlead/ui/help.py` together (`tests/test_help.py` holds them equal): **Start**'s third sentence becomes *It is not a message: a running session is mailed with Message…, a seat still at work is left running beside the members it starts, and a session holding uncommitted or unpushed work refuses the start instead of being closed.*; **not concluded**'s first sentence becomes *Says why this team is not concluded, and so has no Start unless only its seats are live: one clause for each session that keeps it from reading concluded — one that is working, one idle that has not declared, one that crashed or wants a restart, one waiting on your answer to its question.*
+- `ao team start` prints a line per left seat, *left running: techlead-ao-1 (idle, shell live)*, and `--json` carries `left`; the card's toast names them the same way (*started ao-grind — techlead-ao-1 left running*; the seats `left` lists, which may be fewer than the confirm's; *started ao-grind* alone when `left` is empty), in `src/shiftlead/ui/app.py`'s start press, and the Start anyway dialog's second line in `src/shiftlead/ui/static/app.js`.
+- Tests: a team with every member closed and its techlead seat `idle` with `shells_live` reads `members_down` and starts its members without a create for, or a close of, the seat; the same with the manager on call live gives every create that manager's id as its controller; the same started by a session is refused in its own words; a seat closed between the name check and the read is created again; a suspended closed holder still refuses; a live seat the definition renamed keeps the team from `members_down` and refuses the Start as a running orphan; a suspended live seat keeps the team from `members_down`; the same team with a non-seat member live refuses by name; a concluded team still closes its idle seat; Apply's `differences` are unchanged; a live Settings sweeper, and a live worker line's extra, keep the team from `members_down`; a team read concluded at the press though drawn members down closes its idle seat and lists it under `closed`; `members_down` is None on a concluded team; `finished` returns `clauses` matching `why`; `_mark_team_start` writes the mark on a create beside a live seat; the rollup ⋯ holds Start on a members-down team.
+
+**Done when:** On a team whose members are all exited or closed and whose techlead seat is idle with a shell live, the team card offers Start beside Wind down and Stop now, its confirm names the seat it leaves, and the press (or `ao team start`) creates every member and leaves the seat running and untouched; the result lists the seat under `left`.
