+
+**Priority:** Medium
+**Type:** debt
+**Added:** 2026-11-14
+**Owner:** grinder
+**Kind:** build
+**Status:** Open
+**Blocked by:** TD-9001, decision (paul)
+**Part of:** TD-1569
+**Location:** design §4.9a A refused Start says why, §4.9 Starting and stopping; src/shiftlead/teamrun.py (NamesHeld, _close_concluded)
+
+**Why:** TD-1569's second half: `ao team start ao-grind` refused with *techlead-ao-1 is idle … Close it on its card* while the seat was idle with a shell live mid-merge, so the refusal both misread the seat and offered a close that would have cut off its merge.
+
+**Ask:** Go on this build as written, now that TD-1569's four review rounds have ended at the cap (One more round recommended: F91's fix, the suspended verdict never rebuilt, is read by no review)?
+
+**Fix:** Build design §4.9a *A refused Start says why* (the seats the start would leave are not named among the holders) and §4.9 *Starting and stopping*'s refusal words, on TD-9001's `clauses`:
+- `NamesHeld`, on a team that is not concluded, is raised where the records and `waiting_of_home(call, strict=True)` are read (as `_close_concluded` reads them), and names each holder in the launches' order, joined by `; `: a crew record by its clause from `clauses` (person-waiting and reader-waiting included), else by its state and its declaration (*grinder-ao-1 idle, out of work*, *… idle, restart wanted*), else by its state and what it is (*a seat*, *the manager*) — never by the bare `holder_state` alone; a holder not of the team's crew (a person's own session, another team's, no badge, an unrecorded tmux session) and a suspended one keep today's holder words (*<name> is <state> as <holder>*) and are in neither part of the cure, save a person's own session — a session carrying the team's badge with `unattended: false`; one with no badge is not the team's — offered *Close <name> on its card* in the first part where it is `idle` with no subagent or shell live and passes `_unsafe_to_close`. Today's tail (*`ao team stop <team> --close` closes a settled member, or Close it on its card*) is dropped on a team that is not concluded; any refusal on a concluded team keeps today's whole message, its tail included.
+- After a single ` — `, only where it has a part, the cure in two parts, each only where it has a holder: the holders safe to close now: each member of the team's crew (not the manager or a seat) that is `idle`, declared (`out_of_work` or `restart_wanted`), with no `subagents_live` and no `shells_live`, waiting neither on the person nor on a reader, and passing `_unsafe_to_close`; and the person's own session as above — *Close grinder-ao-1 on its card* (never `ao team stop --close`, which would wrap up every live member and seat); then the rest of the crew's holders, *wait for grinder-ao-2, or Wind down*, the two parts joined by `; `; within a part names are joined by `, ` and the last by ` and ` (*Close grinder-ao-1 and grinder-ao-2 on their cards*). A refusal whose holders are all outside the crew ends with their words.
+- The card's toast and `ao team start`'s refusal (exit 1, `{"error": …}` under `--json`) print the same words.
+- Tests: a holder idle with a shell live is named *idle, shell live* and offered no Close; a holder waiting on a reader is offered no Close; an idle undeclared holder is offered no Close; a holder idle, declared and clean is offered Close by name; one safe and one working holder give both parts; an unrecorded tmux holder alone gives today's holder words and no cure; a concluded team's refusal keeps today's tail.
+
+**Done when:** A start refused on a held name names each holder by the clause that keeps the team from concluded (*grinder-ao-1 idle, shell live*), and offers Close only for a holder that is idle with nothing live, not waiting, and clean and pushed.
