+# TD-1569: A team whose members wound down cannot be started from its card while a seat is busy
+
+## What it does
+
+A seat such as the techlead comes on a question and leaves; it is not the team's run. When every member of a
+team is down and only its seats are still live, the team now reads members down. Its card offers Start
+beside Wind down and Stop now, and the Start brings the members back while each running seat carries on with
+what it was doing. A refused Start now says why each session stands in the way, and offers Close only where
+closing is safe.
+
+## The key choices, and why
+
+- It is the same Start, not a second button. The confirm names each seat it leaves running and what it is
+  doing, so the press says what it will not touch.
+- Only a seat the team's definition still names, or an extra of one, is left running. A seat that was renamed
+  or dropped while it ran still blocks the Start, as it does today, so Apply and renames work as before.
+- The Settings sweeper is never left running this way. While it sweeps, its team has no Start: a known gap,
+  left for the sweeper's own design.
+- A team whose idle seats have nothing running is concluded, as before, and its Start closes those seats first.
+- A team with a standing manager live is never members down, since a manager is not one of its seats. The
+  manager is the team's run, and Wind down is its act.
+- Starting with a seat left running is a person's act. A session cannot start its own team's members beside
+  itself.
+- A refusal names each session by what keeps the team from finishing, such as idle with a shell still running.
+  It offers Close only for a member that is idle, has said it is out of work or wants a restart, has nothing
+  running, waits on nobody and has its work pushed, or for your own session. For the rest it says to wait, or
+  Wind down. It no longer suggests stopping the whole team to close one session.
+- From the terminal, your own start leaves the seats running whatever else is live, so it can start a team
+  whose card offers no Start.
+- Two Starts pressed at once are not guarded beyond the session names: each may stop part-way, and every member
+  still starts once.
+- The automatic starts are unchanged. This Start is your press for work the team already saw, members you
+  stopped, or a team set not to start on its own.
+
+## What it rules out
+
+- Closing or cutting off a seat that is still answering someone.
+- A refusal that calls a busy seat idle, or suggests a close that would cut off its work.
+- Two seats doing one job: a renamed seat still running is not left beside its successor.
+
+## What you will see
+
+On ao-grind's card in the case that started this, with only its seats live: members down, the techlead
+seat's state, and Start beside Wind down and Stop now. The confirm reads that the techlead seat is left
+running. After the press the members start and the techlead finishes its merge. A refused Start lists each
+session in its way and what to do about it.
